<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Drives the USB_DEVICE_ATTACHED intent-filter on UsbAttachTrampolineActivity (S12, issue #17):
  when a device matching this filter is physically attached, the platform auto-launches that
  Activity directly, without the user needing to have the app open or tap anything first.

  IDs are DECIMAL, not hex: issue #17's explicit warning, and a very common bug. A hex literal
  here parses and installs without any error, it just silently never matches the real device.
    VID 0x1963 becomes 6499
    PID 0x00D1 becomes 209
  DeviceFilterXmlTest pins these two values against UsbTonexDeviceOpener.VENDOR_ID/PRODUCT_ID by
  parsing this exact file, so a regression here fails a fast JVM test rather than only surfacing
  as "auto-launch silently doesn't happen" on real hardware.
-->
<resources>
    <usb-device vendor-id="6499" product-id="209" />
</resources>
